# Catting absolute paths
>In this challenge, I will not copy it to your home directory, but I will make it readable. You can read it with cat at its absolute path: /flag.

## Solve:
- I first went to the home directory and then used cat to read flag with its path.
```
bash
hacker@commands~catting-absolute-paths:~$ cat /flag
pwn.college{oHhiMdqBomOcVBbzU2V7_WwaHu4.QX5ETO0wiM4ETOwIzW}
```

